// --vm-stats output for tests/run/vm_supers_from.lm (abridged by hand):
// the first list of suggestions is taken, the commented-out one is not,
// and another vm's section is ignored.
== vm stats: W ==
         count       %  op
       1000000   40.0%  ADD
       1000000   40.0%  MUL
        500000   20.0%  NEG

suggested superinstructions (each at least 1% of executed ops; none overlaps another or an
existing super, so they can all be added together):
    super ADD_MUL = ADD; MUL;    // 1000000, 40.0%, saves 1000000 dispatches
    super NEG_RET = NEG; RET;    // 500000, 20.0%, saves 500000 dispatches
    super OLD_NEG = OLD; NEG;    // 10, 1.0%, saves 10 dispatches

also frequent, but each overlaps one of the above or an existing super (an alternative to
it, not an addition):
//  super MUL_NEG = MUL; NEG;    // 500000, 20.0%, saves 500000 dispatches; overlaps ADD_MUL

